 With the same checkpoint, config and packages, a run gives the same episodes
 on every run.
 
+### Check an M* server in the same simulation
+
+`--mstar-url` and `--mstar-client` connect the simulator to an M* Praxis DROID
+server over its Positronic v2 WebSocket. The client module lives in the
+optional server package; local scripted and model runs do not load it. The
+remote run keeps the tasks, scene seeds, camera history and
+result files of this runner. The simulator does not load model weights locally.
+The server must already serve the DROID checkpoint with its Positronic adapter.
+Install the `sim` extra plus `websockets>=12` and `msgpack>=1.0` on the
+simulator host. The server's Positronic config must use
+`observation_format: praxis1` and should put its checkpoint and code revision
+in the ready-frame `meta`, which the runner records with each episode.
+
+```bash
+# One episode, including its MP4 and JSON result.
+MUJOCO_GL=egl python scripts/run_sim_eval.py --suite droid_guard \
+    --mstar-url ws://127.0.0.1:8000/api/v1/session \
+    --mstar-client praxis.serve.sim_client \
+    --tasks lift_cube --sampler-seeds 0 --shard 0/8 \
+    --out outputs/eval/mstar-smoke
+
+# All 56 droid_guard episodes.
+MUJOCO_GL=egl python scripts/run_sim_eval.py --suite droid_guard \
+    --mstar-url ws://127.0.0.1:8000/api/v1/session \
+    --mstar-client praxis.serve.sim_client \
+    --out outputs/eval/mstar-guard
+```
+
+M* Positronic currently chooses the sampler seed for each request. The suite's sampler
+seed still selects the scene schedule and output directory, but it does not
+control M* sampling. A remote run defaults to the suite's first sampler-seed
+label; extra labels requested with `--sampler-seeds` are independent repeats.
+`compare_sim_eval.py` refuses these results because a
+seed-matched paired comparison would be invalid. Use the episode JSON and MP4
+to check closed-loop behavior, and add a shared seed contract before comparing
+M* success rates to the in-process policy as paired episodes. The runner
+records the server meta, command row counts and cold restarts, and refuses to
+resume an output directory made by a different policy or server meta. A local
+`--checkpoint` or `--set model.*`, `sampler.*`, `session.*`, or `policy.*`
+cannot change the server and is refused. If EGL and M* share one GPU, check
+`bad_view_ticks` in each episode JSON for corrupt camera frames.
+
+If Positronic serving is not ready, the benchmark-only openpi adapter can
+smoke-test M*'s 21-row cold mode through the same simulation. It reads the
+root openpi WebSocket, sends the sim pose as an FR3 hand pose, and uses the
+pinned reference conversion to compose relative rows into absolute commands.
+It sends a seed for each call. The runner still marks the result as unpaired
+until the end-to-end seed and recipe parity are checked. The M* deployment
+must use the Praxis DROID openpi schema and `max_context_chunks: 0`.
+
+```bash
+MUJOCO_GL=egl python scripts/run_sim_eval.py --suite droid_guard \
+    --mstar-url ws://127.0.0.1:8000/ \
+    --mstar-client praxis.serve.openpi_sim_client \
+    --tasks lift_cube --sampler-seeds 0 --shard 0/8 \
+    --out outputs/eval/mstar-openpi-cold-smoke
+```
+
+This is a debugging mode. It does not test the 24-row warm session path or
+the production Positronic protocol. A reference cold comparison needs
+`session.max_context_chunks=0`; the ordinary reference suite uses observed
+context instead.
+
+The same cold openpi deployment can be timed once it has a ready metadata
+map with `checkpoint`, `code_version`, `max_context_chunks`, `num_steps`,
+`t_shift`, `cfg_scale` and `cfg_video_scale`. Its request has the same camera
+pixels, pose and prompt as the reference cold request. The openpi adapter
+converts the pose to FR3 hand coordinates and sends the `seed` field. The
+chart labels this as a debugging protocol.
+
+```bash
+python scripts/benchmark_remote_session.py --mode mstar-openpi \
+    --url ws://127.0.0.1:8002/ \
+    --sessions 4 --calls 4 --warmup-sessions 1 \
+    --out outputs/latency/mstar-openpi-cold.json
+python scripts/plot_remote_latency.py outputs/latency/reference-cold.json \
+    outputs/latency/mstar-openpi-cold.json \
+    --out outputs/latency/cold-openpi.svg
+```
+
+### Cold serving latency
+
+`scripts/benchmark_remote_session.py` measures a fixed, raw, one-frame DROID
+observation. It sends sequential calls through the reference's stateless
+chunked server and M*'s cold Positronic server. Each must return 21 command
+rows. The script excludes server startup, handshake and client encoding from
+the round trip time. It requires the ready metadata to identify the checkpoint,
+code version and sampler recipe, and it refuses a warm context. Add those
+values to M*'s `positronic.meta` in the test deployment. The reference server
+receives `context_mode=stateless`, `max_context_chunks=0`, `sample_seed=0` and
+`schedule=chunked` in its URL. M* does not currently accept that seed in its
+Positronic protocol, so these runs measure latency, not output parity.
+
+```bash
+python scripts/benchmark_remote_session.py --mode reference \
+    --url ws://127.0.0.1:8001/api/v1/session \
+    --sessions 4 --calls 4 --warmup-sessions 1 \
+    --out outputs/latency/reference-cold.json
+python scripts/benchmark_remote_session.py --mode mstar \
+    --url ws://127.0.0.1:8002/api/v1/session \
+    --sessions 4 --calls 4 --warmup-sessions 1 \
+    --out outputs/latency/mstar-cold.json
+python scripts/plot_remote_latency.py outputs/latency/reference-cold.json \
+    outputs/latency/mstar-cold.json --out outputs/latency/cold.svg
+```
+
+Run the servers one at a time on the same H200, after each has loaded and
+warmed up. Repeat in reference, M*, M*, reference order in fresh output
+directories to check for drift. Keep the JSON records, the server configs,
+commits and GPU information with the chart. A plot from this client is only
+about cold, sequential, raw-array requests. It says nothing about warm
+episodes, concurrent load or the stock DROID client's JPEG wire.
+
